{
    "background_story": "Corbin was a rugged outdoorsman with a passion for traditional crafts. Growing up in the Scottish Highlands, he was fascinated by the art of hopsacking - weaving sturdy bags from hemp or jute fibers. Corbin spent years perfecting the technique, learning from local elders and experimenting with different patterns. He became renowned for his exceptional hopsacking skills, creating durable and beautiful bags for farmers, fishermen, and travelers. As his reputation grew, Corbin's bags were sought after by collectors and enthusiasts. He continued to innovate, incorporating modern materials and designs while maintaining the traditional techniques that had been passed down through generations. Corbin's dedication to preserving this ancient craft earned him a place in the hearts of his community and the respect of fellow artisans.",
